-- W14 and W15: the block reaches the race.
--
-- Designed backward from race day rather than toward a taper number, so the
-- totals are what the structure produced: W14 lands near 36 against W13's 50,
-- and race week carries 24 before the race for José, 21 for Hope.
--
-- W14's Saturday keeps rhythm and asks nothing. W13's ten miles with four at
-- race pace was the last durability question and it was answered; there is
-- nothing useful left to prove seven days out.
--
-- Race week carries one touch of race pace, three by five minutes, deliberately
-- NOT eligible: we are touching the system, not testing ownership. Hope's
-- carries its own intent, because on 25 August she ran three of four reps under
-- her band and race week is where that costs the most.
--
-- The race IS eligible, and only its 13.1 component is. The warm-up is real
-- running and counts toward the week; it points at no mark. Eligibility is not
-- establishment — authoring the race as eligible awards nothing, and the filed
-- evidence still has to come back inside 6:30–6:45 to establish anything.
--
-- Everything before W14 is untouched.

